<section id="colophon" class="bg-paper border-t border-paper-dark">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-24">

    <div data-reveal class="bg-paper-mid border border-paper-dark rounded-lg p-8 md:p-10">
      <p class="font-body text-xs text-ink-faint uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">
        A note about this site
      </p>
      <p class="font-display text-2xl font-light text-ink mb-4" style="line-height: var(--leading-snug);">
        This portfolio was built the same way.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-base text-ink-muted mb-6" style="line-height: var(--leading-loose); max-width: 58ch;">
        Astro was chosen because it ships zero JavaScript by default — the right tool for a
        content site, not the one I already knew. The design tokens were locked before the
        first page was written. The motion budget was set before the first animation.
        None of that is hidden, because it's the point.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/decisions"
        class="font-body text-sm text-accent hover:text-accent-warm transition-colors"
      >
        Read the decisions, including the ones I turned down →
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
